<p class="report-kicker">Attestward Evidence Pack</p>
<h1>Software Development Security Report</h1>
</div>
</header>

{{if .MappingVersionMismatch}}<div class="note"><strong>Note:</strong> this pack's mapping versions do not match the mapping data used to render this report. Some SSDF task/CISA cluster titles below may be missing or reflect a different revision than what actually produced these results.</div>{{end}}

<section class="report-section" aria-labelledby="executive-summary">
<h2 id="executive-summary">Executive Summary</h2>
<div class="table-wrap">
<table class="key-value-table">
<tbody>
<tr><th scope="row">Org</th><td>{{.Pack.Scope.Org}}</td></tr>
{{if .Pack.Scope.Project}}<tr><th scope="row">Project</th><td>{{.Pack.Scope.Project}}</td></tr>
{{end}}<tr><th scope="row">Repos in scope</th><td>{{range $i, $r := .Pack.Scope.Repos}}{{if $i}}, {{end}}{{$r}}{{end}}</td></tr>
<tr><th scope="row">Scan window</th><td>{{fmtTime .Pack.ScanStartedAt}} &ndash; {{fmtTime .Pack.ScanEndedAt}}</td></tr>
<tr><th scope="row">Tool version</th><td>{{.Pack.ToolVersion}}</td></tr>
<tr><th scope="row">Mapping versions</th><td>SSDF {{.Pack.MappingVersions.SSDF}} &middot; CISA form {{.Pack.MappingVersions.CISAForm}}{{if .Pack.MappingVersions.ScannerSignatures}} &middot; scanner signatures {{.Pack.MappingVersions.ScannerSignatures}}{{end}}{{if .Pack.MappingVersions.SelfAttestation}} &middot; self-attestation {{.Pack.MappingVersions.SelfAttestation}}{{end}}</td></tr>
{{if .Pack.Integrity}}<tr><th scope="row">Pack SHA-256</th><td><code class="hash">{{.Pack.Integrity.SHA256}}</code></td></tr>{{end}}
</tbody>
</table>
</div>

<h3>Cluster status</h3>
<div class="table-wrap">
<table>
<thead><tr><th scope="col">Cluster</th><th scope="col">Status</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
{{range .Clusters}}<tr><td>{{.ID}}. {{.Title}}</td><td class="status-cell">{{if .HasStatus}}<span class="badge badge-{{.Status}}">{{statusBadge .Status}}</span> {{statusLabel .Status}}{{else}}<em>no data</em>{{end}}</td></tr>
{{end}}
</tbody>
</table>
</div>

<h3>Result counts</h3>
<div class="table-wrap">
<table class="counts-table">
<thead><tr><th scope="col">Status</th><th scope="col">Count</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
{{range statusCounts .StatusCounts}}<tr><td class="status-cell"><span class="badge badge-{{.Status}}">{{statusBadge .Status}}</span> {{statusLabel .Status}}</td><td class="numeric">{{.Count}}</td></tr>
{{end}}
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>

<section class="report-section" aria-labelledby="cluster-detail">
<h2 id="cluster-detail">Cluster Detail</h2>
{{range .Clusters}}
<h3>Cluster {{.ID}}: {{.Title}} &mdash; {{if .HasStatus}}<span class="badge badge-{{.Status}}">{{statusBadge .Status}}</span> {{statusLabel .Status}}{{else}}<em>no data</em>{{end}}</h3>
<blockquote>{{.FormText}}</blockquote>

{{range .Tasks}}
<h4>{{.ID}} &mdash; {{if .HasStatus}}<span class="badge badge-{{.Status}}">{{statusBadge .Status}}</span> {{statusLabel .Status}}{{else}}<em>no data</em>{{end}}</h4>
{{if .Text}}<p>{{.Text}}</p>{{end}}

{{range .Checks}}
<div class="check-card" data-status="{{.Status}}">
<div class="check-header">
<div class="check-title">
<span class="check-id">{{.CheckID}}</span>
<h5>{{.Title}}</h5>
</div>
<span><span class="badge badge-{{.Status}}">{{statusBadge .Status}}</span> {{statusLabel .Status}}</span>
</div>
<div class="check-body">
<div class="check-reason"><span class="check-reason-label">Reason</span>{{if .Scope.Repo}}Repo: <code>{{.Scope.Repo}}</code>. {{end}}{{.Reason}}</div>

{{if .Provenance}}<p class="evidence-heading">Evidence</p>
<ul class="evidence-list">{{range .Provenance}}<li><code>{{.Method}} {{.Endpoint}}</code> at {{fmtTime .Timestamp}} (HTTP {{.HTTPStatus}}, digest <code class="hash">{{.ResponseSHA256}}</code>)</li>{{end}}</ul>{{end}}

{{if .Facts}}{{$fv := facts .Facts}}
{{if $fv.Scalars}}<ul class="evidence-list">{{range $fv.Scalars}}<li>{{.Key}}: {{fmtVal .Value}}</li>{{end}}</ul>{{end}}
{{if $fv.Lists}}<ul class="evidence-list">{{range $fv.Lists}}<li>{{.Key}}: {{if .Items}}{{range $i, $item := .Items}}{{if $i}}, {{end}}{{fmtVal $item}}{{end}}{{else}}(none){{end}}</li>{{end}}</ul>{{end}}
{{range $fv.Tables}}<p class="facts-heading">{{.Key}}</p>
<div class="table-wrap"><table class="fact-table">
<thead><tr>{{range .Columns}}<th scope="col">{{.}}</th>{{end}}</tr></thead>
<tbody>{{range .Rows}}<tr>{{range .}}<td>{{fmtVal .}}</td>{{end}}</tr>
{{end}}</tbody>
</table></div>
{{end}}
{{end}}
</div>
</div>
{{end}}
{{end}}
{{end}}
</section>

<section class="report-section" aria-labelledby="gaps">
<h2 id="gaps">Gaps</h2>
{{if .Gaps}}<p>Every <code>verified-fail</code> or <code>partial</code> result, in one place. See poam.md for remediation tracking.</p>
<div class="table-wrap">
<table class="gaps-table">
<thead><tr><th scope="col">POA&amp;M ID</th><th scope="col">Check</th><th scope="col">Repo</th><th scope="col">Status</th><th scope="col">Reason</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
{{range .Gaps}}<tr><th scope="row">{{if .POAMID}}{{.POAMID}}{{else}}&mdash;{{end}}</th><td><code>{{.Result.CheckID}}</code></td><td>{{.ScopeLabel}}</td><td class="status-cell"><span class="badge badge-{{.Result.Status}}">{{statusBadge .Result.Status}}</span> {{statusLabel .Result.Status}}</td><td>{{.Result.Reason}}</td></tr>
{{end}}
</tbody>
</table>
</div>{{else}}<p>No gaps found &mdash; every check that could be verified reported <code>verified-pass</code>.</p>{{end}}
</section>

<section class="report-section appendix" aria-labelledby="self-attested-appendix">
<h2 id="self-attested-appendix">Self-Attested &amp; Not-Checkable Appendix</h2>
<p>Controls in this section were <strong>not independently verified</strong> by this tool &mdash; either the
producer's own claim (self-attested) or a control this tool structurally cannot verify
via API (not-checkable, e.g. plan-gated or no answer on file). Neither status ever
upgrades a CISA form cluster to fully verified.</p>

<h3>Self-Attested</h3>
{{if .SelfAttested}}{{range .SelfAttested}}<div class="check-card" data-status="{{.Result.Status}}">
<div class="check-header">
<div class="check-title">
<span class="check-id">{{.Result.CheckID}}</span>
<h5>{{.Result.Title}}</h5>
</div>
<span><span class="badge badge-{{.Result.Status}}">{{statusBadge .Result.Status}}</span> {{statusLabel .Result.Status}}</span>
</div>
<div class="check-body">
<div class="check-reason"><span class="check-reason-label">Reason</span>{{.Result.Reason}}</div>
{{if .Paired}}<p class="evidence-heading">Complements these API-verified checks</p>
<ul class="evidence-list">{{range .Paired}}<li><code>{{.CheckID}}</code>: <span class="badge badge-{{.Status}}">{{statusBadge .Status}}</span> {{statusLabel .Status}} &mdash; {{.Reason}}</li>{{end}}</ul>{{end}}
</div>
</div>{{end}}{{else}}<p>None.</p>{{end}}

<h3>Not Checkable</h3>
{{if .NotCheckable}}<div class="table-wrap">
<table>
<thead><tr><th scope="col">Check</th><th scope="col">Repo</th><th scope="col">Reason</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
{{range .NotCheckable}}<tr><td><code>{{.Result.CheckID}}</code></td><td>{{.ScopeLabel}}</td><td>{{.Result.Reason}}</td></tr>
{{end}}
</tbody>
</table>
</div>{{else}}<p>None.</p>{{end}}
</section>

<section class="report-section" aria-labelledby="methodology">
<h2 id="methodology">Methodology</h2>
<p><strong>Status definitions:</strong></p>
<div class="status-legend">
<div class="status-definition"><span class="badge badge-verified-pass">{{statusBadge "verified-pass"}}</span> <p><strong>Verified Pass</strong> &mdash; the tool queried the platform API and the returned state satisfies the check's pass condition. Never inferred, only observed.</p></div>
<div class="status-definition"><span class="badge badge-verified-fail">{{statusBadge "verified-fail"}}</span> <p><strong>Verified Fail</strong> &mdash; the tool queried the platform API and the returned state does not satisfy the check's pass condition. Just as definitive as verified-pass.</p></div>
<div class="status-definition"><span class="badge badge-partial">{{statusBadge "partial"}}</span> <p><strong>Partial</strong> &mdash; the tool queried the platform API and got a mixed or incomplete signal: some but not all of a check's sub-conditions hold, or the evidence is suggestive but not conclusive either way.</p></div>
<div class="status-definition"><span class="badge badge-self-attested">{{statusBadge "self-attested"}}</span> <p><strong>Self-Attested</strong> &mdash; no API call can verify this control; the answer comes from the producer's own self-attestation questionnaire, not platform evidence.</p></div>
<div class="status-definition"><span class="badge badge-not-checkable">{{statusBadge "not-checkable"}}</span> <p><strong>Not Checkable</strong> &mdash; the tool could not determine an answer at all (plan-gated, insufficient token permission, or an unanswered self-attestation question). An honest &ldquo;unknown&rdquo;, never inferred as a pass or a fail.</p></div>
</div>

<p><strong>Lookback window:</strong> {{.Pack.Scope.LookbackReleases}} releases / {{.Pack.Scope.LookbackMonths}} months, release tag pattern <code>{{.Pack.Scope.ReleaseTagPattern}}</code>.</p>

<p><strong>What this tool does NOT verify:</strong> developer security training, threat-modeling practice
in depth, documented triage/remediation SLAs beyond what a self-attestation records,
agency-notification process, and any control neither an API call nor the self-attestation
questionnaire can reach. This tool is read-only: it never writes to the scanned platform,
and every claim above traces to either a specific API response (verified-*, partial,
not-checkable) or an explicit producer statement (self-attested) &mdash; never to inference,
and never faked.</p>
</section>

<footer>Generated by attestward {{.Pack.ToolVersion}}. This report is derived entirely from evidence.json; it makes no claims beyond what that file records.</footer>

